# Story 56: Linting (40s)
# Hook: Lint and fix -- the agent runs go vet, staticcheck, and golangci-lint, then cleans up.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-056-linting.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Lint and fix -- the agent runs go vet, staticcheck, and golangci-lint, then cleans up.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Launch rysh inside your project.

[00:08.0 --> 00:13.0]
Double-press Escape for prompt mode.

[00:13.0 --> 00:30.0]
Ask it to lint and fix. The lint tool runs the standard Go linters -- go vet, staticcheck, and golangci-lint -- and returns each finding. Running the linters needs no approval; the agent reads the warnings straight back.

[00:30.0 --> 00:37.0]
As with build and test, the actual code fixes are approval-gated -- you review the diff before any change is written, then it re-lints to verify.

[00:37.0 --> 00:40.0]
Clean code, on request -- linters run, fixes reviewed.

